sub,nileh101,"Harry Niles",1,8,11
com,"Red Sox Manager Lake initially sent up Higgins, a recruit catcher"
com,"up from Columbus, to bat for Donahue but Davis came in from"
com,"first base and complained that Higgins was out of uniform as"
com,"he had a Red Sox home jersey but grey road pants on. A's"
com,"Manager Connie Mack said he had no objection to Higgins"
com,"batting but Umpire Connolly would not allow him to enter the"
com,"game. Higgins never appeared in a game for the Red Sox but"
com,"this player is probably Bob Higgins who caught a few games"
com,"for Cleveland in 1909."
